B3 local definitions (registered in `mission/PHYSICS_BOUNDARY.md` §M). Each is an **explicit formula** in the
background `(g, gi, F, E, Θ)` and the tangent `(h, f, B)`; none is defined as a derivative. IV's `chrVar`, `ricciVar`,
`scalarVar`, `invVar`, `linEinstein`, `linMaxwell`, `linFaraday` are reused unchanged.

* `riemVar`: `δR^a_{bcd} = ∂_c C^a_{db} − ∂_d C^a_{cb} + Σ_e (C^a_{ce}Γ^e_{db} + Γ^a_{ce}C^e_{db} − C^a_{de}Γ^e_{cb}
  − Γ^a_{de}C^e_{cb})` with `C = chrVar` (the expansion `riem_expand` of II's `curv`, varied);
* `riemLowVar`: `δR_{abcd} = Σ_e (h_{ae} R^e_{bcd} + g_{ae} δR^e_{bcd})` (lowering with `g` is varied);
* `weylVar`: variation of V-02's `weyl` keeping `h`, `δRic` (`ricciVar`) and `δR` (`scalarVar`) — no background
  value is used to drop terms;
* `weylFVar`, `ricFVar`, `FfrFVar`: variations of the frame contractions **including all frame factors**, e.g.
  `δ[F(e_A,e_B)] = f(e_A,e_B) + F(b_A,e_B) + F(e_A,b_B)`;
* `brkVar`, `cLVar`, `omLVar`: variations of the commutator `[e_A,e_B]`, of `cL = g(e_C,[e_A,e_B])` (metric varied),
  and of the connection components through the Koszul formula `omL_koszul` (valid for every null frame);
* `HfrVar`, `JfrVar`: variations of `H(e,e,e)` and of `θ^K(J)` (coframe varied by `coVar`).

Bridges (`NPFamily.hasDerivAt_*`): for every `NPFamily` with tangent `(h, f, B)`, the parameter derivative at
`ε = 0` of each registered quantity equals the explicit formula. -/

open Complex Filter Topology
