/-!
# Atlas V-03 (block C): first-order source identities around the Kerr–Newman background

`KNFam M a Q g gi F E Θ W` packages an `NPFamily` whose `ε = 0` member is the KN background of IV / V-01 / V-02
(`gKN`, `giKN`, `faradayKN`, Kinnersley `knE`, `knTh`) with slice `{y | (0, y) ∈ W} ⊆ domReg`. No member with `ε ≠ 0`
is assumed to solve anything. For such a family with tangent `(h, f, B)`, each of V-02's eight off-shell source
identities is differentiated at `ε = 0` (genuine derivatives: the identity holds on the open slice for every `ε`
near `0`); the KN background values (V-02, all proved) then remove exactly the products with a vanishing background
factor. The frame-variation terms `Σ b_A^μ ∂_μ f₀` of the derivatives are kept in the general rule
(`hasDerivAt_fdir_param`) and drop out here only because the differentiated background functions vanish on the open
slice (`hasDerivAt_fdir_param_of_zero`, proved).

The results (`lin_*`) are linear identities among the explicit first variations (`psi*Var`, `kappaVar`, …,
`ricFVar`, `HfrVar`, `JfrVar`, `FfrFVar`) with KN background coefficients. No field equation, gauge or mode condition is
used here; the source terms (`ricFVar`, `HfrVar`, `JfrVar`) are kept. -/

